{"diagnosis": "Fetch test executes 256 NOPs (ADDI x0,x0,0, opcode 7'b0010011) but traps with FAIL 0xdead and TRAP asserted instead of progressing. is_alu_reg_imm never asserts for NOPs so the decoder falls through to illegal-instruction trap. Root cause in excerpt at picorv32.v:877 where is_alu_reg_imm compares to 7'b1010011 instead of 7'b0010011, a bit-6 single-bit opcode error.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -877,1 +877,1 @@
-			is_alu_reg_imm               <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b1010011;
+			is_alu_reg_imm               <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0010011;
", "expected": "tohost PASS, no TRAP: cpu trap asserted, FAIL 0xdead cleared"}

